From: elish-linux-tuning contributors
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250-xiaomi-elish: unlock factory 3.19 GHz Prime OPP

Xiaomi Mi Pad 5 Pro (xiaomi-elish) uses the Snapdragon 870 (SM8250-AC),
whose hardware OSM LUT includes the factory 3187.2 MHz OPP on cpu7.
Without this node in sm8250-xiaomi-elish-common.dtsi, qcom-cpufreq-hw
caps cpu7 at 2.84 GHz (SM8250 / Snapdragon 865 bin).

NOTE: Do NOT apply to non-SM8250-AC devices lacking the 3187.2 MHz bin.
Add this block to arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-elish-common.dtsi
(adjust context if your base tree differs slightly).

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-elish-common.dtsi | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-elish-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-elish-common.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-elish-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-xiaomi-elish-common.dtsi
@@ -1,3 +1,10 @@
+/* Append to sm8250-xiaomi-elish-common.dtsi (root level, after &cpu7_opp_table is defined via sm8250.dtsi): */
+&cpu7_opp_table {
+	opp-3187200000 {
+		opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <3187200000>;
+		opp-peak-kBps = <8368000 51609600>;
+	};
+};
-- 
